   {
    "topic": "ark",
    "side": "critic",
    "date": "Aug 21–26, 2026",
    "title": "Enquirer: Ark ticket sales down over the past decade",
    "body": "The Cincinnati Enquirer reported declining Ark Encounter ticket sales. Ken Ham answered with a 10-minute video that gave no annual figures, citing only \"16 million+\" combined visitors since the Creation Museum opened. AiG's Mark Looy argued in a letter that tickets undercount free children and passholders.",
    "points": [
     "Attendance proxy comes from Williamstown's per-ticket safety fee, obtained by monthly open-records requests",
     "Ham concedes the state tourism incentive ended because its 10-year term expired"
    ],
    "sources": [
     {
      "label": "The Natural Historian (R. Joel Duff), Aug 26",
      "url": "https://thenaturalhistorian.com/2026/08/26/ken-ham-confirms-that-ark-attendance-is-declining/"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "topic": "ark",
    "side": "critic",
    "date": "May 25, 2026",
    "title": "Nine years of Ark attendance below projections",
    "body": "William Trollinger tallies attendance against the 2013 feasibility study, which promised 1.2–2.0 million first-year visitors growing about 4% a year.",
    "points": [
     "Year 1 ≈ 800,000 (50% of projection)",
     "Year 3 peak: 875,882 (51%)",
     "Year 8: 682,101 (27%)",
     "Year 9: 664,813 (26%)",
     "Backed by $62M in Williamstown junk bonds and a $1.825M/yr state sales-tax rebate"
    ],
    "sources": [
     {
      "label": "Righting America",
      "url": "https://rightingamerica.net/sinking-further-and-further-below-their-projections-the-facts-of-ark-encounter-attendance/"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "topic": "ark",
    "side": "critic",
    "date": "Jul 29, 2026",
    "title": "Ark misses its projections, but Kentucky GOP still loves it",
    "body": "Paleontologist Daniel Phelps reports June 2026 sales of 96,004 tickets, up 4,520 from June 2025 but below 2024. An Ark representative told a state tourism committee it draws a million visitors a year, which Phelps disputes.",
    "points": [
     "Adult admission about $55; parking $15; zip lines $59–$144",
     "Sales-tax rebate expires around July 2027"
    ],
    "sources": [
     {
      "label": "The Panda's Thumb",
